**Explanation:**  
This sketch uses the Arduino's internal pull-up resistor (`INPUT_PULLUP`) on the button pin, so the button reads `HIGH` when released and `LOW` when pressed. Software debouncing is implemented by ignoring any state changes that happen within 50 ms of the last detected change, preventing multiple toggles from a single press. Each time the button transitions to `LOW`, the LED state is inverted.

